preConditionHook:
// THE THREE PUSHES ARE ROUGHLY SYMMETRIC IN BOTH PRICE AND TIME -- Grimes's
// qualifier on the three-pushes termination pattern (G03-19, G16-19). The two
// push-to-push increments sit within symmetryTol of each other, and the two
// inter-pivot BAR GAPS sit within timeSymmetryTol bars of each other. The book
// says only "roughly symmetric"; both tolerances are the miner's readings.
//
// A FILTER, NOT A TRIGGER. The pattern itself is ThreePushPattern (shapeMode
// 0) and is not re-authored -- the ThreePush* family already covers detection,
// shape, entry, slope, duration and exit. This is meant to be ANDed beside
// ThreePushPattern or ThreePushReversalEntry in the same pane. Grimes's other
// qualifier, "the third push breaks the trend line drawn across pushes one and
// two", is TrendLineBreak in its own pane.
//
// SIDES FOLLOW ThreePushPattern's: the LONG reads the three swing pivot lows
// (three lower lows, the bottoming pattern) and the SHORT reads the three
// swing pivot highs. Increments are written as POSITIVE magnitudes and BOTH
// are required positive, which is ThreePushPattern's patDn monotonicity
// restated: without it symmetryTol * inc1 can go negative and the band stops
// meaning anything. The duplication with the pane's pattern rule is deliberate
// and keeps this rule self-consistent when placed alone.
//
// NOT ThreePushAcceleration, which is a ONE-SIDED multiple on the same two
// increments, so no setting of it says "the two increments are about equal";
// and nothing in the ThreePush* family measures TIME symmetry --
// ThreePushDurationWindow bounds the pattern's TOTAL bars, not the evenness of
// its legs.
//
// THE TIME TEST IS ON BAR INDICES, a difference of bars-ago counts, so it
// passes the shift test trivially; the price test is a band on a difference of
// differences, likewise.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS HAND-ROLLED, verbatim from ThreePushPattern, rather than
// calling SwingLow(3, ...): Occurrence 3 and above is UNMEASURED in the
// register and the third pivot is the whole point. MEASURED
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot bar is AT
// OR BEYOND the swingStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY BEYOND the swingStrength
// NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER kk the newer bar, so the
// strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is exactly
// swingStrength bars, which is why jj starts there; candidate offsets run
// 0..Length-1 inclusive so jj stops at lookbackBars - 1, while the
// neighbourhood test reaches swingStrength bars PAST the window -- deepest bar
// touched lookbackBars - 1 + swingStrength; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12
// relational tolerance; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured
// high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs. Written
// WITHOUT break, matching the twin statement for statement, and the < 3 guards
// stop a fourth pivot being recorded.
//
// THE SENTINEL IS GUARDED BY THE COUNTS reaching three, never by a price test:
// -1.00 and 0.00 are legitimate prices in a back-adjusted series. The bar
// slots carry -1 too, and they are bar indices, where -1 is safe.
//
// AbsValue is ACCEPTED in the register; std::fabs is its counterpart and
// <cmath> is already included by the emitter.
//
// Every scratch value that must survive the bar is a localVariables entry
// rather than a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement; the loop counters and per-candidate flags are block-scoped.
//
// Deepest bar touched: lookbackBars - 1 + swingStrength.
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)lookbackBars;
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
hiB1 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
hiB3 = -1.0;
loB1 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
loB3 = -1.0;
for (int jj = pivS; jj <= pivW - 1; ++jj) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int kk = jj - pivS; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + pivS; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) { hiPx1 = high[jj]; hiB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[jj]; hiB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[jj]; hiB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) { loPx1 = low[jj]; loB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[jj]; loB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[jj]; loB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
}
dnInc1 = loPx3 - loPx2;
dnInc2 = loPx2 - loPx1;
dnBars1 = loB3 - loB2;
dnBars2 = loB2 - loB1;
upInc1 = hiPx2 - hiPx3;
upInc2 = hiPx1 - hiPx2;
upBars1 = hiB3 - hiB2;
upBars2 = hiB2 - hiB1;
symDn = (nLoPiv >= 3) && el_gt(dnInc1, 0.0) && el_gt(dnInc2, 0.0)
    && el_le(std::fabs(dnInc2 - dnInc1), symmetryTol * dnInc1)
    && el_le(std::fabs(dnBars2 - dnBars1), timeSymmetryTol);
symUp = (nHiPiv >= 3) && el_gt(upInc1, 0.0) && el_gt(upInc2, 0.0)
    && el_le(std::fabs(upInc2 - upInc1), symmetryTol * upInc1)
    && el_le(std::fabs(upBars2 - upBars1), timeSymmetryTol);
